Package: xios-session-stubs
Name: Xios GNOME session bridges
Version: 0.2.8
Architecture: @DEB_ARCH@
Maintainer: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Author: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Depends: libglib2.0-0, libiosexec1 (>= 1.3.1), ldid
Recommends: pulseaudio-utils
Section: X11
Priority: optional
Description: iOS-backed freedesktop D-Bus services for the Xios GNOME session
 Small GLib/GIO daemons that provide the freedesktop system services a
 GNOME session expects but that have no daemon on jailbroken iOS:
 .
   xios-login1-stub    org.freedesktop.login1     session/seat/user/inhibitors
   xios-polkit-stub    org.freedesktop.PolicyKit1 auto-allow (single-user root)
   xios-accounts-stub  org.freedesktop.Accounts   persistent single-user profile
   xios-bluez-stub     org.bluez                  BlueZ D-Bus API over iOS BluetoothManager
 .
 xios-bluez-stub is an ObjC daemon that owns org.bluez and answers the subset of the
 BlueZ 5 ObjectManager / Adapter1 / Device1 API gnome-bluetooth uses (the backend of
 the GNOME Settings Bluetooth panel and the shell Bluetooth quick-toggle), backed by the
 private BluetoothManager.framework. It lists the device's real paired/connected Bluetooth
 devices and reflects adapter power/discovery. Signed with com.apple.bluetooth.system (the
 entitlement bluetoothd's XPC peer-check requires). Pairing is wired through BluetoothDevice;
 agent ownership, aliases, trust state, and device removal are tracked by the bridge, with final
 new-device validation pending on hardware.
 .
 The package also owns the minimal xios-setsid session launcher and all GNOME
 session descriptors. Launching a session validates these artifacts instead of
 generating executable helpers or mutating library/schema trees at runtime.
 .
 They implement the Manager/Session/Seat/User calls gnome-session,
 gnome-settings-daemon, Mutter, libpolkit and libaccountsservice actually make, and
 hold no real power (there is no VT, seat or logind to manage). login1 and accounts
 report the real logged-in user, resolved from the passwd entry and the device's
 MobileGestalt name. Accounts profile edits persist in the Xios data directory and emit
 the standard AccountsService change notifications.
 .
 Also ships xios-sysintd (from native-bundle) when built: it bridges the iPad
 hardware volume buttons to the desktop PulseAudio sink (via pactl, hence the
 pulseaudio-utils recommendation) and applies the iOS light/dark appearance to the
 GTK color-scheme. Installed to @INSTALL_PREFIX@/libexec; launch-gnome-session.sh
 brings all of them up on the session bus before starting the shell. See the
 gnome-session plan in the Xios docs. Target profile: @REPO_PROFILE@.
